          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "```java\n/**\n * Tests reusing a parser to process new string records one at a time as they\n * are being discovered. See CSV-110.\n *\n * @throws IOException if an I/O error occurs\n */\n@Test\npublic void testGetOneLineOneParser() throws IOException {\n    try (java.io.PipedReader reader = new java.io.PipedReader();\n            java.io.PipedWriter writer = new java.io.PipedWriter(reader);\n            CSVParser parser = new CSVParser(reader, CSVFormat.DEFAULT)) {\n\n        final String[] inputs = { CSV_INPUT_1, CSV_INPUT_2 };\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < inputs.length; i++) {\n            writer.write(inputs[i]);\n            writer.write('\\n');\n            writer.flush();\n\n            final CSVRecord record = parser.nextRecord();\n            assertNotNull(record);\n            assertEquals(RESULT[i].length, record.size());\n            for (int j = 0; j < RESULT[i].length; j++) {\n                assertEquals(RESULT[i][j], record.get(j));\n            }\n            assertEquals((long) i + 1, record.getRecordNumber());\n        }\n\n        writer.close();\n        assertNull(parser.nextRecord());\n    }\n}\n```"
        }
      ],
